      "text": "Twin Valley earned its name from the valley where the Wild Rice River meets a smaller stream.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twin_Valley%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area now known as Heiberg Park was the original settlement that became Twin Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.twinvalleymn.com/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Norwegian settler Heiberg bought a mill from Olsen and helped build a flour mill that sparked the village’s growth in 1880.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
